{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G12", "modalite": "référence-interne", "appui": "(no values - this is the control)", "doute": false}
{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G13", "modalite": "présent", "appui": "most LDPC codes use block sizes of hundreds or thousands of bits, which means thousands of different variables that need to be tracked […] Instead I decided to use BCH codes", "doute": false}
{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G14", "modalite": "trois-éléments", "appui": "I tested all these on GPT-6 Astra with 100 trials, using 7 variables and 300 dots (filler tokens)", "doute": false}
{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G15", "modalite": "aucune", "appui": "", "doute": false}
{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G16", "modalite": "phrase", "appui": "This doesn't really prove that Astra is doing a form of belief propagation.", "doute": false}
{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G17", "modalite": "dispersées", "appui": "I think I'm reaching the limits of what I can learn with only black-box access and no architectural details", "doute": false}
{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G18", "modalite": "mentionnées", "appui": "Curiously, when I tried explicitly prompting for marginal probabilities, the results became less accurate!", "doute": false}
{"codeur": "C1", "billet": "B685128", "geste": "G19", "modalite": "posée-et-contrôlée", "appui": "To reduce the chance of benchmark contamination issues, I'm randomizing the BCH code construction rather than using standard ones.", "doute": true}
